  "notes": "The 1999–2001 supergroup, and the entry states the split cleanly: \"the rhythm grid is hip-hop; the harmony and vocals are soul\". So the drums are the sampler-and-live blend it describes — \"an SP-1200/MPC-lineage looped break under a played kick and tambourine, snare hard on 2&4, hats crisp in 16ths\" — which is a layered snare, a high kick density and the loudest hat velocities in this batch, over a modest offGrid window because the break itself is quantised. The band is the entry's 88–110. Harmony carries no numerals — \"major-mode funk with dominant-7th and 9th colour; short 2-to-4-bar cycles, blues-scale melodic overlay, and no modulation\" — so no families are authored and the delta is a dominant-weighted extension spread, `maxChords` 3 and a vamp-leaning harmonic rhythm; the blues-scale overlay is in `scales` and `halfStepDissonance`. Melody is \"short-phrase, riff-like, high note-density on the hook\" with \"call-and-response male/female lead trading\" as the arrangement's identity, so the structure is call-and-response and the counter is dense at −12. Bass is Saadiq's, \"mixed forward, syncopated and melodic, occasionally doubled by a filtered synth-sub\". ⚠ The INFERRED parameters are all drum probabilities and velocities and every melody number; the research marks its parametric detail as lane inference and its tempo band [LOW-CONF]. ⚠ The synth-sub double is not authored as a `bass808` block — it doubles a played bass rather than replacing it.",
